msgid "Management interface reference"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Various Quarkus extensions contribute non-application endpoints that provide "
"different kinds of information about the application.\n"
"Examples of such extensions are the xref:smallrye-health.adoc[health], xref:"
"telemetry-micrometer.adoc[metrics], xref:openapi-swaggerui.adoc[OpenAPI] and "
"xref:info.adoc[info] extensions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"These non-application endpoints are normally accessible under the `/q` "
"prefix like so:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`/q/health`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`/q/metrics`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`/q/openapi`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`/q/info`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, these management endpoints are served by the same HTTP server as "
"your application endpoints.\n"
"This document presents how you can use a separate HTTP server (bound to a "
"different network interface and port) for the management endpoints.\n"
"It avoids exposing these endpoints on the main server and, therefore, "
"prevents undesired accesses."
msgstr ""

msgid "Enabling the management interface"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To enable the management interface, use the following **build-time** "
"property:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, management endpoints will be exposed on: `http://0.0.0.0:9000/q`."
"\n"
"For example, if you have `smallrye-health` installed, the readiness probe "
"will be exposed at `http://0.0.0.0:9000/q/health/ready`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"SmallRye Health Checks, Micrometer and Info endpoints will be declared as "
"management endpoints when the management interface is enabled."
msgstr ""

msgid "Configure the host, port and scheme"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, the management interface is exposed on the interface: `0.0.0.0` "
"(all interfaces) and on the port `9000` (`9001` in test mode).\n"
"It does not use TLS (`https`) by default."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can configure the host, ports, and TLS configuration name using the "
"following properties:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.management.host` - the interface / host"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.management.port` - the port"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.management.test-port` - the port to use in test mode"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`quarkus.management.tls-configuration-name` - the TLS configuration name, "
"xref:http-reference.adoc#using-the-tls-centralized-configuration[same as for "
"the main HTTP server]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Here is a configuration example exposing the management interface on _https:/"
"/localhost:9002_:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With this configuration, TLS is enabled and configured as defined in the "
"`management` configuration of the TLS registry."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can also configure the management interface with the legacy SSL "
"configuration, as for (xref:http-reference.adoc#ssl[the main HTTP server]):"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Key store, trust store and certificate files can be reloaded periodically.\n"
"Configure the `quarkus.management.ssl.certificate.reload-period` property to "
"specify the interval at which the certificates should be reloaded:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The files are reloaded from the same location as they were initially loaded "
"from.\n"
"If there is no content change, the reloading is a no-op.\n"
"It the reloading fails, the server will continue to use the previous "
"certificates."
msgstr ""

msgid "Configure the root path"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Management endpoints are configured differently than standard HTTP endpoints."
"\n"
"They use a unique root path, which is `/q` by default.\n"
"This management root path can be configured using the `quarkus.management."
"root-path property`.\n"
"For example, if you want to expose the management endpoints under `/"
"management` use:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The mounting rules of the management endpoints slightly differ from the ones "
"used when using the main HTTP server:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Management endpoints configured using a _relative_ path (not starting with `/"
"`) will be served from the configured root path.\n"
"For example, if the endpoint path is `health` and the root path is "
"`management`, the resulting path is `/management/health`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Management endpoints configured using an _absolute_ path (starting with `/`) "
"will be served from the root.\n"
"For example, if the endpoint path is `/health`, the resulting path is `/"
"health`, regardless of the root path"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The management interface does not use the HTTP root path from the main HTTP "
"server."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `quarkus.http.root-path` property is only applied to the main HTTP "
"server and not to the management interface.\n"
"In addition, the `quarkus.http.non-application-root-path` property is not "
"used for endpoint exposed on the management interface."
msgstr ""

msgid "Create a management endpoint in an extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"SmallRye Health Checks, and Micrometer endpoints will be declared as "
"management endpoints when the management interface is enabled."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Extensions can create a management endpoint by defining a _non application_ "
"route and calling `management()` method:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the management interface is enabled, the endpoint will be exposed on: "
"`http://0.0.0.0:9000/q/my-path`.\n"
"Otherwise, it will be exposed on: `http://localhost:8080/q/my-path`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Exposing an endpoint on the management interface (as an application)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can expose endpoints on the management interface by registering routes "
"on the management router.\n"
"To access the router use the following code:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `io.quarkus.vertx.http.ManagementInterface` event is fired when the "
"management interface is initialized.\n"
"So, if the management interface is not enabled, the method won't be called."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `router()` method returns a `io.vertx.ext.web.Router` object which can "
"be used to register routes.\n"
"The paths are relative to `/`.\n"
"For example, the previous snippet registers a route on `/admin`.\n"
"This route is accessible on `http://0.0.0.0:9000/admin`, if you use the "
"default host and port."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"More details about the `Router` API can be found on https://vertx.io/docs/"
"vertx-web/java/[the Vert.x Web documentation]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Management Interface Configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid "Running behind a reverse proxy"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus can be accessed through proxies that generate headers (e.g. `X-"
"Forwarded-Host`) to preserve information about the original request.\n"
"Quarkus can be configured to automatically update information like protocol, "
"host, port and URI to use the values from those headers."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To set up this feature for the management interface, include the following "
"lines in `src/main/resources/application.properties`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To constrain this behavior to the standard `Forwarded` header (and ignore `X-"
"Forwarded` variants) by setting `quarkus.management.proxy.allow-forwarded` "
"in `src/main/resources/application.properties`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can prefer `X-Forwarded-*` headers using the following "
"configuration in `src/main/resources/application.properties` (note `allow-x-"
"forwarded` instead of `allow-forwarded`):"
msgstr ""

msgid "Supported forwarding address headers are:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`Forwarded`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`X-Forwarded-Proto`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`X-Forwarded-Host`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`X-Forwarded-Port`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`X-Forwarded-Ssl`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`X-Forwarded-Prefix`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If both header variants (`Forwarded` and `X-Forwarded-*`) are enabled, the "
"`Forwarded` header will have precedence."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Ensure that your proxy is configured to strip unexpected `Forwarded` or `X-"
"Forwarded-*` headers from the client request."
msgstr ""

msgid "Kubernetes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When Quarkus generates the Kubernetes metadata, it checks if the management "
"interface is enabled and configures the probes accordingly.\n"
"The resulting descriptor defines the main HTTP port (named `http`) and the "
"management port (named `management`).\n"
"Health probes (using HTTP actions) and Prometheus scrape URLs are configured "
"using the `management` port."
msgstr ""

msgid "KNative"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Until https://github.com/knative/serving/issues/8471[KNative#8471] is "
"resolved, you cannot use the management interface, as KNative does not "
"support containers will multiple exposed ports."
msgstr ""

msgid "CORS filter"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To make your Quarkus management interface accessible to another application "
"running on a different domain, you need to configure cross-origin resource "
"sharing (CORS).\n"
"For more information about the CORS filter that Quarkus provides, see the "
"Quarkus xref:security-cors.adoc#cors-filter[CORS filter] section of the "
"\"Cross-origin resource sharing\" guide."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The management interface uses the same CORS filter mechanism as the main "
"HTTP server, but with separate configuration under `quarkus.management.cors."
"*`."
msgstr ""

msgid "For example, to allow requests from a specific origin:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When CORS is enabled without configuring specific origins, only same-origin "
"requests are allowed."
msgstr ""

msgid "HTTP Host header validation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The management interface supports the same HTTP `Host` header validation as "
"the main HTTP server, but with separate configuration under `quarkus."
"management.host-validation.*`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When `quarkus.management.host` is set to a localhost name (`localhost`, `127."
"0.0.1`, or `[::1]`), host validation is automatically enabled in **dev** and "
"**production** modes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This automatic behavior is a change from previous Quarkus versions.\n"
"If the management interface is accessed through a reverse proxy or a non-"
"localhost host name, configure the allowed hosts explicitly or disable "
"automatic validation."
msgstr ""

msgid "For example, to restrict requests to specific host names:"
msgstr ""

msgid "To disable automatic localhost validation:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more details on the available options and reverse proxy considerations, "
"see the xref:http-reference.adoc#host-header-validation[HTTP Host header "
"validation] section in the HTTP reference guide."
msgstr ""

